WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Transmission. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Relate gear teeth, speed and torque

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: A gear pair trades rotational speed for torque in the ideal model. A real transmission adds stages and mechanical losses.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: 18-tooth driver to 54-tooth driven gear: ratio 3:1; 3,000 rpm input becomes 1,000 rpm output ideally.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Ratio calculation

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: Ideal mechanism only; friction, heat and part-specific behavior need measurements.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Relate gear teeth, speed and torque
